    "text": "To solve for the value of \\(6 \\star 5\\) using the operation defined by \\(K \\star L = (K+L)(K-L)\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the values of \\(K\\) and \\(L\\) from the expression \\(6 \\star 5\\). Here, \\(K = 6\\) and \\(L = 5\\).\n2. Substitute \\(K = 6\\) and \\(L = 5\\) into the operation definition \\(K \\star L = (K+L)(K-L)\\).\n\nFirst, calculate \\(K + L\\):\n\\[\nK + L = 6 + 5 = 11\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(K - L\\):\n\\[\nK - L = 6 - 5 = 1\n\\]\n\nNow, multiply the results of \\(K + L\\) and \\(K - L\\):\n\\[\n(K+L)(K-L) = 11 \\times 1 = 11\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(6 \\star 5\\) is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).",
